# Kitchen starch hunt: flour and dough are not just white powders
#
# Lugol solution is brown without starch and blue-black when its iodine meets
# sufficiently long starch helices. Use separate cups so that each sample sees
# the same water and indicator dose. Iodine stains: protect eyes, clothes and
# the work surface, and do not taste any laboratory mixture.
register lv1

# A sugar control. White does not mean starch.
add v1 water 100mL
add v1 granulated_sugar 2g
add v1 lugol_solution_1_percent 2mL
look v1

# Flour resolves a reviewed starch fraction, so the same computed absorption
# band appears without a special-case claim about flour.
new beaker
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 flour 2g
add v2 lugol_solution_1_percent 2mL
look v2

# Plain flour-and-water dough carries the same starch identity.
new beaker
add v3 water 100mL
add v3 flour_water_dough 3g
add v3 lugol_solution_1_percent 2mL
look v3

# The colour identifies starch; it does not measure how much is present. This
# bench also does not model cooking, starch gelatinisation or food safety.
